# Binding-tail host preparation — unexecuted

This source-only capsule prepares one original/candidate correctness differential. Root owns review, exact leaf materialization, the future host seal, execution, source restoration and any promotion decision. Neither request is closed by this preparation. No native, performance or campaign acceptance credit exists.

The actual subject is `scripts/combat/authored_enemy_sequence.gd`, original SHA `9aed90b797bdef3388a82b63f40390e2b779f2fec671ed3914a33b1ff42950a3`, mode `0644`. Candidate bytes stay inert in the producer capsule. Root must inspect the final 265-line renderer-hook-v2 leaf, its successor review and original `PLAN.json`, then copy that exact inert leaf to the v2 producer's sibling `.gd` target named in `INPUT_SPEC.json`. Earlier v1 stays unselected and unexecuted. This host never materializes the leaf or imports resources. Its UID must remain genuinely absent.

After review and materialization, Root may choose these commands from the canonical checkout:

```sh
python3 .cinder/runtime-next-binding-tail-host-prepare-20261016/run.py seal
python3 .cinder/runtime-next-binding-tail-host-prepare-20261016/run.py pair --seal /absolute/path/from/the/closed/seal/phase/seal.json
```

These are proposed future commands, not execution authorization. Seal is host-only. Pair waits for the existing canonical `dev.godot_lock`, without a queue deadline or bypass. It runs one original child, closes and indexes that phase, swaps only the canonical subject under the same held lock, runs one candidate child with the identical selected leaf, then restores the original bytes and mode in `finally` before releasing the lock. Each child uses the actual canonical Script identity, canonical `ProjectContext` and `run_validation`; timeout is 180 seconds after acquisition, with the leaf's 90-second native watchdog. No full suite, import, renamed class or accepted-state shortcut is used.

Original bytes are durably retained before any swap. The pair writes queued, at-lock, after-child, before-swap, after-swap, after-restore and runner-close source maps, modes/types and bounded input CAS. Every phase has separate command, raw stream, engine log, actual native report if produced, result, report joins and closed index. Missing or incomplete native reports remain missing/incomplete. Engine binary SHA/size/mode are observed before/after without copying the 351 MB executable. Source closure is explicit and bounded; it is not a claim to freeze all dynamic loading or every installed engine component.

Canonical validation returns are labeled as API results. The current API does not independently expose the OS child's status; timeout 124 or script-error 1 may be synthetic. Logs preserve all diagnostics. A complete passing native original with API return 0 may permit the one candidate cell even if its raw stream contains a warning/CA diagnostic. That original still closes Host 2 NONCLEAN, and the overall pair cannot pass cleanly. A functional original failure stops before candidate. There is no same-cell rerun for a green result.

Cross-phase comparison requires exact ordered `observations` plus opaque `initial_wire_exact`, using JSON text that preserves bool/int and int/float distinctions. Variant/source SHA are separate metadata. Native functional checks, clean host status and semantic equality remain separate facts. This is correctness evidence only; no timing fields or performance claim.

The selected leaf and transitive bounded sources contain no `user://`, network or child-process calls. The only native write in that closure is the fresh report path supplied inside this capsule's owned output. Difficulty/equipment JSON opens are read-only. The inherited arena constructs native floor/obstacle/Scheduler objects directly; `project.godot` has no autoload, and `--script` replaces the campaign main scene. No user Store or process-specific user-data directory is needed. Root should use the default sandbox.

Cooperative SIGINT/SIGTERM cleanup restores inside the lock. SIGKILL, host crash or power loss cannot run Python `finally`. The durable original backup/receipt exists for Root recovery under the canonical queue lock; never delete another process's lock or kill another worker. Unexpected subject bytes are retained separately before the owned original restoration and force failure. Byte/mode restoration does not claim original inode or modification time.

Preparation host checks use only private temporary files and a fake canonical API. They do not execute Godot, import canonical dev, swap production sources, create a seal or produce native credit. `HOST_TESTS.json` records their actual outcome. All execution remains unexecuted until Root selects it.
